.TH MAILHUB 1 "2026-09-22" "Mailhub 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
mailhub \- Local Mailhub administration
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B mailhub
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fICOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mailhub
is the administration CLI for Mailhub, a local personal-operations hub for AI
assistants. It manages configuration, OAuth credentials, account health, and
exposes a loopback-only REST API and stdio MCP server.
.PP
All provider calls use official APIs (Gmail, Microsoft Graph) or standard
protocols (IMAP/SMTP, CalDAV, CardDAV). Configuration and credentials are
stored locally with restrictive permissions.
.SH OPTIONS
The following global options are available for all commands:
.TP
\fB--config\fR \fIPATH\fR
Configuration file path (default: \fI~/.config/mailhub/config.toml\fR).
.TP
\fB--state\fR \fIPATH\fR
Credential state file path (default: \fI~/.local/state/mailhub/credentials.json\fR).
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
\fBinit\fR
Create owner-only local configuration and state files with correct permissions
(0600). Generates bearer tokens for REST API access.
.TP
\fBauth\fR \fIPROVIDER\fR \fIALIAS\fR [\fB--code\fR \fICODE\fR]
Authorize an account via OAuth flow. \fIPROVIDER\fR is \fBgmail\fR or
\fBgraph\fR. \fIALIAS\fR is the account alias from config. If \fB--code\fR
is provided, exchange the authorization code or redirect URL directly.
.TP
\fBstatus\fR
Show configured accounts and their capabilities without contacting providers.
.TP
\fBdoctor\fR
Check account health, refresh tokens, and report status (ok, needs_reauth,
invalid_credentials, etc.).
.TP
\fBreauth\fR \fIPROVIDER\fR \fIALIAS\fR
Re-authorize an account, forcing a new consent screen. Use when scopes have
changed or tokens are revoked.
.TP
\fBlogout\fR \fIALIAS\fR
Remove stored tokens for an account. Configuration entry remains.
.TP
\fBserve\fR [\fB--host\fR \fIADDR\fR] [\fB--port\fR \fIPORT\fR]
Start the REST API server. Binds to \fB127.0.0.1\fR only (default port 8787).
.TP
\fBmcp\fR [\fB--mode\fR \fIMODE\fR]
Run the stdio MCP server. \fIMODE\fR is \fBro\fR (read-only, default) or
\fBfull\fR (read-write). M1 supports read-only mode only.
.TP
\fBconfig\fR \fISUBCOMMAND\fR [\fIARGS\fR...]
Manage Mailhub configuration.
.SH CONFIG SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
\fBconfig list\fR
List all configured accounts with their providers and capabilities.
.TP
\fBconfig add-account\fR [\fB--alias\fR \fIALIAS\fR] [\fB--provider\fR \fIPROVIDER\fR] [\fB--capabilities\fR \fICAP\fR...] [\fB--email\fR \fIEMAIL\fR]
Interactively add a new account, or non-interactively with flags.
.TP
\fBconfig validate\fR
Validate config syntax and provider credentials.
.TP
\fBconfig doctor\fR
Validate config structure and check account health (same as top-level
\fBdoctor\fR).
.TP
\fBconfig setup-google\fR
Open browser to Google Cloud Console for OAuth client setup, then prompt for
Client ID and Secret.
.TP
\fBconfig setup-microsoft\fR
Open browser to Microsoft Entra ID for app registration, then prompt for
Application (client) ID.
.TP
\fBconfig remove-account\fR \fIALIAS\fR
Remove an account from configuration and its stored tokens.
.SH FILES
.TP
\fI~/.config/mailhub/config.toml\fR
Account definitions, provider credentials, and settings (mode 0600).
.TP
\fI~/.local/state/mailhub/credentials.json\fR
Refresh tokens, OAuth state, and generated bearer tokens (mode 0600).
.TP
\fI~/.local/state/mailhub/audit.jsonl\fR
Audit log for mutating actions (never records tokens or message bodies).
.SH EXAMPLES
.TP
Initialize configuration and add a Gmail account:
.B mailhub init
.br
.B mailhub config setup-google
.br
.B mailhub config add-account
.br
.B mailhub auth gmail personal
.TP
Start the REST server and use the mail CLI:
.B mailhub serve
.br
.B mail accounts
.br
.B mail search personal "is:unread"
.TP
Check account health:
.B mailhub doctor
.TP
Run read-only MCP server:
.B mailhub mcp --mode ro
